    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d193-a1">

                <pb facs="0546" n="524" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v2/pg524"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 58.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Earl Granville to
                        General Schenck.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-05-20"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 20,
                        1872</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: We agree that it might save time, in case
                    of the Treaty being adopted, if I were to prepare a form of notes from Her
                    Majesty’s Government and the Government of the United States, communicating the
                    Treaty to the Tribunal of Arbitration at Geneva.</p>
                <p>I therefore send you the draught which I have prepared.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with the highest consideration, sir, your most obedient,
                    humble servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GRANVILLE.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
